From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 08:36:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Windows: one MIDR a processor on iOS, so CPUID counts every
 core

iOS gives user space no MIDR, so the iOS branch of FetchHostFeatures
added a single entry to CPUMIDRs. CPUIDEmu takes its core count from
the number of entries, so the guest was told of one core: leaf 1
EBX[23:16] was 1, every leaf 4 subleaf said 1 core, and 0x80000008 ECX
said 1, while GetSystemInfo and GetLogicalProcessorInformationEx said
6 on a 2 P + 4 E iPhone (PLA-392; the cputopo probe, both x86-64 and
i386). A title that counts cores by CPUID would size its work for one.

Add one entry for each processor GetSystemInfo reports, all with the
same Apple MIDR as before, so CPUID's counts match the processor count
(madeira.cfg's cpu-count included, since it sets that count). The
entries are equal, so the hybrid flag stays off, and the per-CPU brand
string is the same on every processor.

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-19-cpu-topology-phone.md
Offered-upstream: no; the single entry is the iOS port's (fex-port)
---
 Source/Windows/Common/CPUFeatures.cpp | 12 +++++++++---
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Source/Windows/Common/CPUFeatures.cpp b/Source/Windows/Common/CPUFeatures.cpp
index 8eee381..66639f0 100644
--- a/Source/Windows/Common/CPUFeatures.cpp
+++ b/Source/Windows/Common/CPUFeatures.cpp
@@ -132,9 +132,15 @@ FEXCore::HostFeatures CPUFeatures::FetchHostFeatures(bool IsWine, FEXCore::HostF
                       HostFeatures.SupportsAtomics, HostFeatures.SupportsFlagM, HostFeatures.SupportsFlagM2,
                       HostFeatures.SupportsFCMA, HostFeatures.SupportsAES, HostFeatureControl());
   }
-  // iOS gives no MIDR to user space: one entry, with Apple's implementer (0x61)
-  // and part 0, which CPUID's brand string names "Apple Silicon" on every core.
-  HostFeatures.CPUMIDRs.push_back(0x6100'0000u);
+  // iOS gives no MIDR to user space: one entry a processor, each with Apple's
+  // implementer (0x61) and part 0, which CPUID's brand string names "Apple
+  // Silicon" on every core. CPUID's core counts (leaf 1 EBX[23:16], leaf 4,
+  // 0x80000008) are the number of entries, so there is one for each processor
+  // GetSystemInfo reports (PLA-392); with a single entry the guest was told of
+  // one core.
+  SYSTEM_INFO SystemInfo {};
+  GetSystemInfo(&SystemInfo);
+  HostFeatures.CPUMIDRs.resize(SystemInfo.dwNumberOfProcessors ? SystemInfo.dwNumberOfProcessors : 1, 0x6100'0000u);
   HostFeatures.HostType = HostType;
   HostFeatures.ProcessPID = ProcessPID;
   return HostFeatures;
